chet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T00:00:56-07:00","id":1322168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1321914-can-werewolves-be-targeted-for-spirit-claiming-or-possession?p=1322103#post1322103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bearing in mind that pretty much every conceivable step in the process is contested, laying the groundwork is expensive, and werewolves are generally better-equipped to recognize when they're being subjected to spiritual influence, yes, werewolves are not specifically immune to possession or Claiming.<br /> <br /> What makes <i>idigam</i> with the Forge Empty Wolf Essence-Shaping power particularly terrifying is that they can make an Empty Wolf all in one go at no special cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>And also nothing says that the spirit they stuff into a werewolf can't be themselves. Idigam are scary, y'all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> T